* BEH-IC-RS232-DIP16 B1: driver levels with 3 kohm load to GND (RS-232 test load), Vcc=5 V; TIN low -> OUT positive, TIN high -> negative.
* v2: scalars printed as 'name = value'; behavior unchanged
* Pump: VS+ = 2*5-1.0 - 200*I ; unloaded driver level = VS+-1.0. Load: V = (VS+-1)*3000/(3000+300) ... solve with pump drop: I = V/3k (ignoring other current)
*  VS+ = 9 - 200*I ; V = (VS+ - 1.0)*3000/3300  -> V = (8 - 200 V/3000)*0.90909 -> V = 7.2727 - 0.060606 V  -> V = 6.857 V ; (negative side symmetric: -6.857 V), VS+ = 9 - 200*2.286 mA = 8.54 V
* TI SLLS047N extract: 'high level output voltage 5..7 V typ at RL=3k'. 
.include max232.lib
Vcc vcc 0 5
Vh t1h 0 0
Vl t1l 0 5
X1 c1p vsp c1m c2p c2m vsm t2o r2i r2o t2i t1h r1o r1i o1 0 vcc max232
X2 d1p vsp2 d1m d2p d2m vsm2 t2o2 r2i2 r2o2 t2i2 t1l r1o2 r1i2 o2 0 vcc max232
Rl1 o1 0 3k
Rl2 o2 0 3k
Rg1 t2i 0 1k
Rg2 t2i2 0 1k
Rg3 r2i 0 1k
Rg4 r2i2 0 1k
Rg5 r1i 0 1k
Rg6 r1i2 0 1k
.control
set noaskquit
op
let vo1 = v(o1)
let vo2 = v(o2)
let vsp_ = v(vsp)
let vsm_ = v(vsm)
echo v_out_tin_low_v = $&vo1
echo v_out_tin_high_v = $&vo2
echo vs_plus_v = $&vsp_
echo vs_minus_v = $&vsm_
quit
.endc
.end
